  "worked_solution": "We need to isolate $x.$ To do this, we first cross-multiply:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12nx}{2} & =\\frac{4}{7} \\\\ 7\\cdot 12nx & =2\\cdot 4 \\\\ 84nx & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides of the equation by $84n:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84nx & =8 \\\\ \\frac{84nx}{84n} & =\\frac{8}{84n} \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{84n}x}{\\cancel{84n}} & =\\frac{8}{84n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{8}{84n}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can further simplify the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{4\\cdot 2}{4\\cdot 21n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 2}{\\cancel{4}\\cdot 21n} \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{21n}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
